            <ArticleTitle>A Case Report of Candida albicans Costochondritis after a Complicated Esophagectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e608</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/GOX.0000000000000599</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present an unusual case of Candida albicans costochondritis after a complicated Ivor Lewis esophagectomy. This case exhibits that pain, erythema, and swelling over the costal cartilages should alert the possibility of infective costochondritis, especially in a postoperative patient. If a fungal agent is identified, aggressive surgical debridement and early commencement of antifungal therapy are likely determinants for a satisfactory outcome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
